#
# ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'
#

pmc:TranserfingSharedAsKnownTruth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Claims cannot be proven; offered as known truth"@en, "Behauptungen unbeweisbar; als gewusste Wahrheit angeboten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says he cannot prove this point by argument, nor anything in the book; he shares what he knows to be true, and only the reader can know whether it resonates."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStagesOfIllness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of illness in an epidemic"@en, "Stadien der Erkrankung in einer Epidemie"@de ;
    skos:definition "Illness is said to stem from voluntarily agreeing to play the 'Epidemic' game: rumours, acceptance of possible infection, imagining being sick (which tunes thought energy to the pendulum), selective attention and self-delivering confirmation, a strengthening bond, and finally acceptance at first symptoms, which shifts one to a line where illness prevails."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAcceptingThePossibility a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Accepting the possibility of falling ill"@en, "Die Möglichkeit des Erkrankens annehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Rumour of a flu going round leads one to take for granted that one might catch it and to picture oneself ill in bed; from that moment imagination tunes one's thought energy to the destructive pendulum and one plays its game."@en ;
    skos:note "First member of pmc:TranserfingStagesOfEpidemicIllness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConfirmationArrives a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Confirmation arrives by itself"@en, "Die Bestätigung kommt von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The subconscious looks for proof that the epidemic is coming, attention turns selective, sneezing people seem to be everywhere and the topic keeps coming up; the evidence arrives of its own accord even without searching."@en ;
    skos:note "Second member of pmc:TranserfingStagesOfEpidemicIllness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingActiveAdherent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming an active adherent of the illness"@en, "Aktiver Anhänger der Krankheit werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Tuned to the pendulum from the start, one's bond with it grows whether or not one takes part consciously; not minding the idea of illness, or feeling bound to catch something, makes one an active adherent."@en ;
    skos:note "Third member of pmc:TranserfingStagesOfEpidemicIllness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFinalAdjustment a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Final adjustment to the line of illness"@en, "Letzte Einstimmung auf die Linie der Krankheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "After a feeble attempt to resist at the first symptoms, one accepts that one will be ill; this completes the change of one's energy vibration and one passes onto a line on which illness is common."@en ;
    skos:note "Last member of pmc:TranserfingStagesOfEpidemicIllness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfPersuasionFails a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-persuasion of health fails"@en, "Selbstüberredung zur Gesundheit scheitert"@de ;
    skos:definition "Repeatedly telling oneself that one is perfectly healthy does not work: merely thinking about the illness, positively or negatively, tunes one to its frequency, and the effort reinforces acceptance of likely illness."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: self-persuasion of health fails, bearing on pmc:TranserfingStagesOfIllness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFaithOutweighsWords a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Faith outweighs words"@en, "Glaube überwiegt Worte"@de ;
    skos:definition "Spoken words are warm air and inner words nothing compared with silent faith, whose power is inaudible; lacking it, even a vaccination is said not to protect, and one is ill as long as one needs to be."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingQuickRecoveryChosen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Quick recovery chosen at first symptoms"@en, "Schnelle Genesung bei ersten Symptomen gewählt"@de ;
    skos:definition "The first symptoms are said to offer a choice between falling seriously ill and recovering very quickly."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStagesOfEpidemicIllness a pm:Sequencing ;
    rdfs:label "Stages of illness in the epidemic game"@en, "Stufen der Erkrankung im Spiel Epidemie"@de ;
    skos:definition "The stages of disease as the source unfolds them: accepting the possibility, confirmation arriving, becoming an active adherent, the choice at the first symptoms, and the final adjustment that shifts one to a line of illness."@en ;
    skos:note "The text announces these as the stages of disease. The fourth place is the capacity pmc:TranserfingQuickRecoveryChosen, the choice the first symptoms offer. No consequence of skipping a stage is named, so no pm:Presupposing pairs are entered."@en ;
    rdf:_1 pmc:TranserfingAcceptingThePossibility ;
    rdf:_2 pmc:TranserfingConfirmationArrives ;
    rdf:_3 pmc:TranserfingActiveAdherent ;
    rdf:_4 pmc:TranserfingQuickRecoveryChosen ;
    rdf:_5 pmc:TranserfingFinalAdjustment ;
    pm:seriesStatement "Illness is the end of a game one agreed to at the start: each stage deepens the tuning begun by the one before, and only at the first symptoms is the choice between quick recovery and serious illness still open, after which acceptance seals the shift." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingShiftBeginsAtResponse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Induced shift begins at the response"@en, "Induzierter Übergang beginnt mit der Reaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "The induced shift starts at the very moment one responds to the pendulum's prod."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnaffectedByEpidemic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being unaffected by an epidemic"@en, "Von einer Epidemie unberührt bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Someone who genuinely does not care about an epidemic, or knows nothing of it (on holiday, no news, little contact), is said not to be affected; the pendulum vanishes for them. Doctors working unmasked are cited as not infected because they play a different role in the illness pendulum's game; flight attendants likewise."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoDogma a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing is no dogma"@en, "Transurfing ist kein Dogma"@de ;
    skos:definition "Epidemic claims are a general tendency; the author does not call infection a delusion nor thought energy the sole cause of illness. Transurfing is not a dogma or final authority; no idea is absolute truth; only patterns and regularities can be considered."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Epidemic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Panic'
#

pmc:TranserfingPanicTransition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Panic as the fastest induced transition"@en, "Panik als schnellster induzierter Übergang"@de ;
    skos:definition "Panic produces the most intense and rapid induced transition: real danger signals sound convincing so the spiral coils hard and fast; the panicking person loses self-control and becomes receiver and transmitter of the swing; the pendulum uses panic to materialize in the crowd. In panic one hardly thinks of overcoming the pendulum."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Panic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingKeepingOnesHead a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Keep your head and look around"@en, "Den Kopf behalten und sich umsehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a panic, keep composure and take a second to look around (e.g. notice the empty lifeboats beside the crowded ones), resisting the whirlpool that sucks in its periphery."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Panic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSavingOneselfInPanic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Saving oneself and others in panic"@en, "Sich und andere in der Panik retten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping one's head is said to make it possible to save oneself and others."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Panic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeepingOnesHeadYieldsSavingOneselfInPanic a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Composure yields rescue"@en, "Besonnenheit bewirkt Rettung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Keeping one's head lets one see the overlooked way out."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingKeepingOnesHead ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSavingOneselfInPanic ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Panic'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'
#

pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Becoming rich from poverty"@en, "Aus der Armut reich werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The text treats a shift from a life line of poverty to one of prosperity as attainable, contrasting it with the obstacles that hold people on the line of poverty."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAchievingTheImpossible a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Achieving what seems impossible"@en, "Erreichen des scheinbar Unmöglichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing, not fitting common sense, is said to enable things that would otherwise seem impossible, such as a poor man becoming rich."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingThreeThoughtsOfPoverty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Despising poverty, envying the rich, wishing to be better off"@en, "Armut verachten, Reiche beneiden, sich Besseres wünschen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With contempt for one's poverty, envy of the wealthy and constant wishing to be better off, a shift to a prosperous line is very hard, the author says totally impossible."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: despising poverty, envying the rich, wishing to be better off, bearing on pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhatYouHateFollowsYou a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "What you hate follows you"@en, "Was man hasst, verfolgt einen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Hating something makes one think of it and radiate at the frequency of lines where it abounds; polarity does not matter, though dislike gives the pendulum more energy; active hatred creates excess potential, and balancing forces act against the individual since removing one opponent is easier than changing the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingUravnoveshivayushchieSily."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReadinessBeforeGetting a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Readiness to act before getting what one wants"@en, "Handlungsbereitschaft vor dem Erlangen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Without being prepared to act to acquire what one wants, one does not get it."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step is intention, the readiness to act (pmc:TranserfingNamerenie)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingNamerenie ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "One will not obtain what one wants." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWishDeemedUnrealistic a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Belief that the wish is unrealistic"@en, "Überzeugung, der Wunsch sei unrealistisch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The poor typically fail to act because they are convinced their desire cannot be fulfilled, a vicious circle that keeps them where they are."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: belief that the wish is unrealistic, bearing on pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNamerenie a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Intention, not desire, is the moving force"@en, "Absicht, nicht Wunsch, ist die bewegende Kraft"@de ;
    skos:definition "Desire on its own has no power and cannot even lift a finger; intention, defined as readiness to act, is what lifts it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWantingVersusReadiness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gap between wanting and readiness to become"@en, "Kluft zwischen Wollen und Bereitsein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wanting is far from being ready to become: a poor person feels out of place among the wealthy because at heart they feel unworthy; wealth lies outside their comfort zone through unfamiliarity rather than discomfort, and their emitted frequency clashes with the frequency of a rich life."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingAdmittingWealthIntoComfortZone a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Admit wealth into the comfort zone"@en, "Reichtum in die Komfortzone lassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Let the attributes of wealth into one's comfort zone and learn what it feels like to own expensive things, so that wealth stops being unfamiliar."@en ;
    skos:note "Only stated as a requirement here; no stepwise procedure in this section."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingComfortZoneBeforeWealth a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Comfort zone before wealth"@en, "Komfortzone vor Reichtum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Wealth requires first admitting its attributes into the comfort zone."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingAdmittingWealthIntoComfortZone ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Poverty persists even after finding hidden treasure; a windfall is squandered." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAdmittingWealthIntoComfortZoneYieldsRagsToRiches a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Comfort-zone widening yields wealth"@en, "Erweiterung der Komfortzone bewirkt Reichtum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Familiarity with wealth's attributes is presented as what lets a person cease being poor."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingAdmittingWealthIntoComfortZone ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEnvyBlocksWealth a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Envy blocks wealth through subconscious rejection"@en, "Neid blockiert Reichtum durch unbewusste Ablehnung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Envy is purely destructive: one devalues what the other has to console oneself, the wish turns into defence and then rejection, and the subconscious, taking everything literally, works to ensure one never receives what was devalued."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: envy blocks wealth through subconscious rejection, bearing on pmc:TranserfingRagsToRiches."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLiteralSubconscious a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Subconscious takes everything literally"@en, "Das Unbewusste nimmt alles wörtlich"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conscious mind merely plays at devaluing, but the subconscious takes it in earnest and acts on it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInducedPoverty a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Induced transition into poverty"@en, "Induzierter Übergang in die Armut"@de ;
    skos:definition "The spiral unwinds slowly then accelerates: temporary financial trouble; disappointment (weak energy); anger and resentment let the pendulum suggest a culprit; negative talk or action starts the second turn (lower income, price rises, debts called in); the person sees bad luck where a directed process runs, their vibration moves to lines of deprivation; destructive conversations, anxiety and excess potential follow, balancing forces join, and finally the adherent is flung off, having lost much or everything, and is dropped by the pendulum. It needs negative energy, not money. Groups can undergo it too."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingNotReactingToMoneyTrouble a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Do not react emotionally to temporary financial difficulties"@en, "Auf vorübergehende Geldnot nicht emotional reagieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Treat temporary money trouble like rain on a picnic day: do not get angry, depressed, overly anxious or resentful, and do not grab the spiral's tail; if the response stops at mild disappointment, the pendulum is stilled."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotReactingToMoneyTroubleYieldsStoppingThePendulum a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Non-reaction to money trouble stills the pendulum"@en, "Nichtreaktion auf Geldnot bringt das Pendel zur Ruhe"@de ;
    skos:definition "Deprived of energy, the pendulum of financial difficulty comes to rest."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingNotReactingToMoneyTrouble ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingStoppingThePendulum ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAngerRevivesPendulum a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Anger and resentment revive the pendulum"@en, "Ärger und Groll beleben das Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Going beyond disappointment to anger and resentment, blaming others and acting against them revives the pendulum and sets the spiral's second coil going."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: anger and resentment revive the pendulum, bearing on pmp:TranserfingNotReactingToMoneyTrouble."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnawareOfTheProcess a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unawareness that a process is running"@en, "Nicht bemerken, dass ein Prozess läuft"@de ;
    skos:definition "At the second turn the person usually takes the losses for bad luck, not realising a directed process was induced by their emotional response."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: unawareness that a process is running, bearing on pmc:TranserfingInducedPoverty."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCollectiveWhirlpool a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Collective induced transition cannot be escaped"@en, "Kollektiver induzierter Übergang ist unentrinnbar"@de ;
    skos:definition "When a large group undergoes the transition to poverty, the spiral becomes a massive whirlpool from which escape is impossible."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingInducedPoverty ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Constant awareness: keep the inner Guardian awake"@en, "Ständige Bewusstheit: den inneren Wächter wach halten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Do not grab the spiral's tail; keep constant awareness of pendulums and do not let the inner Guardian doze. Each time you notice you have habitually, as in a dream, accepted a pendulum's game (voiced discontent, indignation, anxiety, joined a destructive discussion), pull yourself up. Treat everything that provokes a negative reaction as a destructive pendulum's provocative prod; wake up from the game as from a dream."@en ;
    skos:note "The inner Guardian named here is pmc:TranserfingInnerGuardian (part 2); in this chapter it is the watcher that must not doze off, so that one notices having slipped into a pendulum's game."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingConstantAwarenessYieldsFreeOfThePendulumsPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Awareness yields freedom from pendulums"@en, "Bewusstheit bewirkt Freiheit von Pendeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Constant awareness and self-correction keep one out of induced transitions."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAwarenessBeyondKnowing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing the mechanism is not enough"@en, "Kenntnis des Mechanismus reicht nicht"@de ;
    skos:definition "Understanding how induced transitions work is insufficient; constant awareness is required to stay free."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingConstantAwareness ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without awareness one acts out of habit as in a dream, stays a pawn in another's game, open to being tormented like by nightmares." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Remaining free of the pendulums' power"@en, "Frei von der Macht der Pendel bleiben"@de ;
    skos:definition "By staying aware one is said to remain outside the destructive pendulum's game, be in control and no longer a victim of circumstances while others continue in a zombie-like state."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGameAsUnrecognisedDream a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulum game as an unrecognised dream"@en, "Pendelspiel als unerkannter Traum"@de ;
    skos:definition "Like a dreamer who is a pawn and prey to nightmares until realising it is a dream, one is a victim of circumstances until one wakes up to the nature of the game; then one is in control."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. V The Induced Transition, section 'Poverty'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'
#

pmc:TranserfingWorldMeetsYouHalfway a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Going with the flow makes the world meet you halfway"@en, "Mit dem Strom gehen: die Welt kommt entgegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Chapter epigraph: one who goes with the flow is met halfway by the world."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Chapter epigraph; developed in section 'Going With the Flow'."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingInformationFieldMatrix a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alternatives space as information field and energy matrix"@en, "Variantenraum als Informationsfeld und Energiematrix"@de ;
    skos:definition "The alternatives space is described as an information field, an energy matrix serving as a pattern of the possible; a sector illuminated by energy of the same resonance turns into physical reality."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingProstranstvoVariantov."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSubconsciousReadsTheField a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Subconscious accesses the field directly"@en, "Das Unbewusste greift direkt auf das Feld zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "The conscious mind cannot read the field but the subconscious (the soul) can; premonitions, intuition, prophecies, inventions and art originate there, and reason then translates the data into word and symbol."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTruthAndKnowledge a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Truth in the field, knowledge in the mind"@en, "Wahrheit im Feld, Wissen im Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Data in the information field is pure, undistorted truth, a record of everything that moves matter by natural law; passing through the mind's filter it becomes interpretation, i.e. knowledge, which is always more or less distorted and differs between beings."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOldBricks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind builds only from old bricks"@en, "Der Verstand baut nur aus alten Ziegeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reason can combine familiar objects and logic to solve problems, but cannot directly access fundamentally new information; discoveries, inventions, music, art and poetry come from insight and inspiration received by the soul, and only later become property of the mind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAgainstConventionalWorldview a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Against fundamental science and the conventional worldview"@en, "Gegen die Grundlagenwissenschaft und das herkömmliche Weltbild"@de ;
    skos:definition "The pendulums of fundamental science are said to refuse to take paranormal phenomena seriously so as not to reveal their impotence; inability to explain them neither makes them unreal nor justifies dismissal. The conventional view that reason alone synthesises the new is called a product of an attitude and as unprovable as Transurfing."@en ;
    skos:note "Polemic of the author against a view he describes himself; only his side is read, so it is entered as a concept and not as pm:Disputing."@en ;
    skos:note "Opponent is generic (fundamental science, conventional worldview), not a named author."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClairvoyance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Clairvoyant perception of the field"@en, "Hellseherische Wahrnehmung des Feldes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Some people are said to perceive field events with the clarity of material ones, past, future or distant, by attuning to manifested sectors, e.g. locating a missing person via a photo or belongings; police are said to use them."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:thirdPartyAscription ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWhyClairvoyantsErr a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why clairvoyants err"@en, "Warum Hellseher irren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Clairvoyants err by attuning to sectors never realised and never to be realised, and because nearby sectors vary in their script and scenery, which distorts interpretation; ancient prophets read future scenes with the knowledge of their time, so their predictions were inaccurate."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: why clairvoyants err, bearing on pmc:TranserfingClairvoyance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUsableModelNotSecret a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Transurfing as a usable model, not the secret"@en, "Transurfing als nutzbares Modell, nicht das Geheimnis"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing is only a model for applying the universe's laws to one's own interests; it claims no complete description of the universe and is no monument revealing the secret; truth is only ever nearby. What matters is that information from the alternatives space reaches us as hunches, visions, insights and signs whose meaning we must try to grasp."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Information Field'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'
#

pmc:TranserfingNewIsHardToReceive a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Why the fundamentally new is hard to receive"@en, "Warum grundlegend Neues schwer zu empfangen ist"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only rare individuals read the field; most get echoes as fleeting premonitions and vague knowing. New insights take years because thought energy attunes more easily to already realised sectors, while the fundamentally new lies in unrealised ones, and how to attune to these is still unknown."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUnrealisedSectorObscure a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Unrealised-sector information seems obscure"@en, "Information aus unverwirklichten Sektoren wirkt dunkel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Data from an unrealised sector confuses the conscious mind because it has never been rendered in familiar symbols; if the brain penetrates its essence, insight and clarity result."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReasonAndHeart a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Reason versus heart/soul"@en, "Verstand gegenüber Herz/Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "For simplicity the author assigns everything of the conscious mind to 'reason' and everything of the subconscious to 'heart' or 'soul'."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindDoesNotListen a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind does not listen to the heart"@en, "Der Verstand hört nicht auf das Herz"@de ;
    skos:definition "If reason understood all the heart offers, humanity would have full access to the field; but the mind, absorbed by the outer world and its incessant inner monologue of thought and worry, is inattentive to the heart's faint signals and insists on its own way, thinking in categories that mark qualities of materialised sectors."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDesignationsAndDiscovery a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Designations and the birth of discovery"@en, "Bezeichnungen und die Geburt der Entdeckung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reason decodes everything through established designations (symbols, words, concepts, rules); information from a non-materialised sector without a designation is felt as unfathomable knowledge, and a discovery happens when new designations are found or it is fitted into existing references. Like a first hearing of music, it is at once knowledge and mystery; a child learns categories by being shown, not told."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartFeelsAndKnows a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart feels and knows without categories"@en, "Das Herz fühlt und weiß ohne Kategorien"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart neither thinks nor speaks but feels and knows; ever since the mind took to abstract categories the heart-mind connection has atrophied, so the mind struggles to grasp what the heart cannot put into words."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReleasingControlForIntuition a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing control lets intuition through"@en, "Kontrolle lösen lässt Intuition durch"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind's chatter and urge to control drown the heart's vague signals; once the mind's control is loosened, intuitive feelings and knowledge can reach consciousness."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRustleOfTheMorningStars a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Rustle of the morning stars as the inner voice"@en, "Rauschen der Morgensterne als innere Stimme"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart's signals arrive as an ambiguous premonition, the inner voice, perceptible when the mind is distracted: wordless voice, thoughtless reflection, soundless sound; one knows one has understood something yet it stays elusive. Everyday intuitions (sensing a visitor, foreseeing an event, simply knowing) are of this kind."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingContemplatingEmptiness a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Stop thoughts and contemplate emptiness"@en, "Gedanken anhalten und die Leere betrachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Think less, feel and listen to intuition: halt the stream of thinking and just regard the emptiness, so that the wordless inner voice is no longer drowned by thought-churn."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingContemplatingEmptinessYieldsHearingTheMorningStars a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Contemplating emptiness yields hearing the inner voice"@en, "Leere betrachten bewirkt Hören der inneren Stimme"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stopping the thought stream is said to make the morning-stars rustle audible."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingContemplatingEmptiness ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHearingTheMorningStars ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingComfortAsForesight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart's comfort and discomfort as foresight"@en, "Wohl und Unbehagen des Herzens als Vorausschau"@de ;
    skos:definition "The heart has two discernible states, comfort and discomfort. Having access to the field, it sees impending but unrealised sectors and knows whether they will be pleasant; the mind registers this as vague inner peace or its absence."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartRarelyWrong a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The heart is rarely wrong"@en, "Das Herz irrt selten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The soul often knows what is coming and patiently signals it, but the pendulum-hooked, problem-solving mind barely hears it or dismisses it and decides by logic, which guarantees no ideal solution; the heart, not thinking, is rarely mistaken (hence hindsight claims of having known)."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Heart check before a decision"@en, "Herzensprüfung vor einer Entscheidung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Instruct the inner Guardian to watch your inner state before a final decision. If you remember, note what you feel: anything that alerts, worries or displeases you. After making a decision, have the mind fall silent briefly and check whether it feels good or bad; next picture the other decision and ask the same question again."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartCheckYieldsKnowingTheUnrealisedSector a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heart check yields foreknowledge"@en, "Herzensprüfung bewirkt Vorwissen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Comparing the felt response to alternative decisions reveals what the unrealised sector holds."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowingTheUnrealisedSector ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeartCheckYieldsHearingTheMorningStars a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heart check yields hearing the morning stars"@en, "Herzensprüfung bewirkt Hören der Morgensterne"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simply remembering to note one's inner condition is said to suffice for perceiving the morning-stars rustle."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingHearingTheMorningStars ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBanalButWorking a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Banal but working"@en, "Banal, aber wirksam"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author concedes the heart check sounds trivial and commonplace but asserts that it works; the only difficulty is attending to feelings, which people have unlearned by trusting reason over the sense of wholeness that inner calm brings."@en ;
    skos:note "Said of pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoClearFeeling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "No clear feeling: the mind is not yet listening"@en, "Kein klares Gefühl: der Verstand hört noch nicht zu"@de ;
    skos:definition "If no clear feeling emerges, the mind is still poor at listening; the remedy is to have the inner Guardian alert one to one's inner state more often."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: no clear feeling: the mind is not yet listening, bearing on pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoDecisionOnAmbiguity a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not decide on an ambiguous question"@en, "Bei mehrdeutiger Frage nicht entscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "The vagueness may lie in the question itself; then one should not decide on vague information but to rely on the mind's judgement or simplify the question."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingClearYesOrNo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A clear yes or no feeling"@en, "Ein klares Ja- oder Nein-Gefühl"@de ;
    skos:definition "A distinct sense of feeling good or not good about the option shows one has clearly caught the morning-stars rustle and knows the answer, even if circumstances do not always let one follow it."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: a clear yes or no feeling, for pmp:TranserfingHeartCheck."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnowingTheUnrealisedSector a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Knowing what an unrealised sector holds"@en, "Wissen, was ein unverwirklichter Sektor bereithält"@de ;
    skos:definition "By reading the heart at decision time one is said to foresee what a sector not yet turned into physical reality holds, i.e. whether a choice will feel good or bad."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Knowledge Out of Nowhere'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'
#

pmc:TranserfingExtremesAndRoles a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Paper boat versus rowing against the tide; needy, indignant, fighter"@en, "Papierboot gegen Rudern wider den Strom; Bittsteller, Empörter, Kämpfer"@de ;
    skos:definition "Two extreme responses to any situation: drifting powerlessly with the current or rowing stubbornly against it. Those who give up responsibility take the path of the needy or the indignant; the fighter rows against the tide; Transurfing proposes a further stance."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPassivityMakesAPuppet a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Passivity makes one a pendulum's puppet"@en, "Passivität macht zur Marionette eines Pendels"@de ;
    skos:definition "A lazy, goalless person content to exist is controlled by other forces and easily becomes a pendulum's puppet; believing fate predestined, they are proved right, because that route too is present as a possibility in the alternatives space."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheNeedy a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The needy role"@en, "Die Rolle des Bittstellers"@de ;
    skos:definition "The needy accept circumstances and beg from a pendulum or a higher power; the pendulum makes them toil for a meagre living. Expecting God to see to one's needs personally combines abdication of responsibility with self-importance; freedom of choice is said to be God's ultimate gift, refused by the infantile."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObstaclesFromSelfImportance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obstacles stem from self-importance"@en, "Hindernisse stammen aus Selbstwichtigkeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "The 'something' that always goes wrong for people is balancing forces and pendulums arising from the excess potential of their self-importance."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheIndignant a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The indignant role"@en, "Die Rolle des Empörten"@de ;
    skos:definition "The indignant voice dissatisfaction and demand what they think they are owed, damaging their potential destiny further; they forget they are merely guests in this world, and punishment only deepens their resentment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGoAheadAndGetIt a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Getting what one wants without pleading, demanding or struggling"@en, "Bekommen, was man will, ohne Bitten, Fordern, Kämpfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Transurfing's path: if you want something, neither beg nor demand nor fight for it, simply go and take it; obstacles are said to fade away."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfDeterminationTooFar a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Self-determination taken too far becomes struggle"@en, "Überzogene Selbstbestimmung wird zum Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "People often overdo the stance of making their own choices: they declare war on pendulums, compete, elbow forward, and life becomes a struggle for survival, which is played out because it too exists as a possibility."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingGoAheadAndGetIt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHowRolesCreatePotential a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How the needy and indignant create excess potential"@en, "Wie Bittsteller und Empörte Überschusspotenzial erzeugen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Passive acceptance and open dissatisfaction both make one dependent on pendulums: the needy create excess potential through guilt and hand themselves to manipulators; the indignant through continual dissatisfaction, endlessly invoking balancing forces."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTheFighter a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The fighter wastes energy and entrenches the struggle myth"@en, "Der Kämpfer verschwendet Energie und festigt den Kampfmythos"@de ;
    skos:definition "The fighter is more productive but lives hard; resisting entangles them further in the web, energy is squandered, and occasional costly wins reinforce the belief that success must be fought for."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: the fighter wastes energy and entrenches the struggle myth, bearing on pmc:TranserfingGoAheadAndGetIt."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceAsFeedingTrough a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance as the pendulums' feeding trough"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit als Futtertrog der Pendel"@de ;
    skos:definition "Public opinion is shaped by pendulums, which feed on excess potential born of self-importance. The belief that a goal is hard to reach projects outer importance; the belief that only an extraordinary personality can reach it projects inner importance. Most energy goes not on the goal but on the pendulum's exactions, like pushing through a crowd of beggars."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReducingImportanceYieldsFreeOfThePendulumsPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance yields freedom from pendulums"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit aufgeben bewirkt Freiheit von Pendeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "Breaking the loop by abandoning importance makes the pendulums leave one in peace."@en ;
    skos:note "Here the reducing of inner and outer importance (pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance, taught in part 2) is invoked as breaking the loop with pendulums, after which the scroungers turn to someone else."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReducingImportanceYieldsGoAheadAndGetIt a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Dropping importance yields getting without struggle"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit aufgeben bewirkt Erlangen ohne Kampf"@de ;
    skos:definition "With importance gone, obstacles fade and one can simply go and take what one wants."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingGoAheadAndGetIt ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceBeforeGetting a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Freedom from importance before going and getting"@en, "Freiheit von Bedeutsamkeit vor dem Nehmen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Being able to take one's goal without asking, demanding or struggling is presented as following on abandoning inner and outer importance."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingGoAheadAndGetIt ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'The Needy, the Indignant and the Fighter'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'
#

pmc:TranserfingNoRoleGivesFreedom a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "None of the three roles gives freedom"@en, "Keine der drei Rollen gibt Freiheit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Needy and indignant drift limply, the fighter shoves against the current; everyone mixes these roles, none is effective. A rational mind can still be steered by thought patterns created by pendulums, so in these roles there is no freedom of movement; the fighter is no freer than the paper boat, whipping the water where calm strokes would do."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Being at the helm"@en, "Am Steuer stehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ideal stance: neither fighting the current and stirring eddies nor drifting like a paper boat, but moving deliberately in tune with the current, watching for sandbanks, obstacles and danger zones and keeping one's chosen course with smooth movements."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTechenieVariantov a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Alternatives flow"@en, "Variantenfluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "Information in the alternatives space is static, matrix-like, yet arranged as causal chains; these chains give rise to the flow of alternatives, which is what Transurfing means by flow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeitherResistNorSurrender a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Neither resist nor surrender wholly to the flow"@en, "Dem Fluss weder widerstehen noch sich ihm ganz überlassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Resisting the flow wastes huge energy in vain or to one's harm; but relying entirely on it is also unsafe, as it may carry one into a calm lagoon or to a waterfall's edge. Proceed cautiously, correcting with smooth actions."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSettingTheGeneralCourse a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Setting the general course"@en, "Den allgemeinen Kurs festlegen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Know which way one's flow runs overall, a direction fixed by the goal one has chosen and the means of reaching it; once that course is fixed, lean on the current as far as possible and correct one's movement with smooth actions."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the integrator as the prior step of pmc:TranserfingCourseBeforeFlow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCourseBeforeFlow a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Set the general course, then rely on the flow"@en, "Erst die Richtung festlegen, dann dem Fluss vertrauen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The general direction of one's flow is fixed by one's chosen goal and the means to reach it; once this course is set, one ought to lean on the current wherever one can."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step, fixing the general course by goal and means, is entered as pmp:TranserfingSettingTheGeneralCourse."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingSettingTheGeneralCourse ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAstrologyNotNegated a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Astrology and clairvoyance not negated"@en, "Astrologie und Hellsehen nicht verneint"@de ;
    skos:definition "Though astrological calculation and clairvoyance are not fully accurate, the Transurfing model does not deny their worth since forecasting and seeing draw on the alternatives space; were their hit rate too low, nobody would take them seriously. The flow also allows a glance at other physically realised sectors. Reliance on forecasts is left a personal matter."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImportanceMakesRapids a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Importance turns the flow into rapids"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit macht den Fluss zu Stromschnellen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Inner and outer importance is the main source of trouble, making balancing forces appear as rapids and whirlpools on one's path; reducing it calms the current. Outer importance drives the mind to complicated solutions of simple problems, inner importance convinces it that its reasoning alone is right."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFreeMind a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A mind free to decide objectively"@en, "Ein Verstand, frei für sachgerechte Entscheidungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "With projected importance reduced, the mind is said to breathe freely, be released from pendulums and artificial problems, and make more objective, fitting decisions without needing a powerful intellect; everyday problems need far less energy."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReducingImportanceYieldsFreeMind a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Reducing importance frees the mind"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit senken befreit den Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Lowering inner and outer importance yields a mind able to decide objectively."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeMind ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProblemsResolveThemselves a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Problems resolving themselves"@en, "Probleme lösen sich von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "The flow is said to contain the solutions to all problems; most problems are artificially created by a mind prodded by pendulums, and most, especially minor ones, resolve on their own if the flow is left to run."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOptimalityPrinciple a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Optimality principle of the field"@en, "Optimalitätsprinzip des Feldes"@de ;
    skos:definition "Optimality is built into the information field: cause-and-effect chains form streams that are the best paths; although everything exists, the most energy-efficient alternative is likeliest to be realised, as nature never wastes energy; streams follow the path of least resistance, where the optimal solution lies. The pendulum-influenced mind loses the flow in a maze of complicated solutions."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingTestInPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Test it in practice"@en, "In der Praxis prüfen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author grants that these notions may seem conjectural and invites the reader to try the ideas in practice and decide for themselves whether the flow exists."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKeysToAnyProblem a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Access to the keys of any problem"@en, "Zugang zu den Schlüsseln jedes Problems"@de ;
    skos:definition "The flow is said to encode the keys to every problem, accessible by learning to go the way of least resistance."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingSimplestWay a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Choose the simplest solution; do everything the easiest way"@en, "Die einfachste Lösung wählen; alles auf dem leichtesten Weg tun"@de ;
    skos:definition "Make a habit of picking the simplest possible solution to every problem; under the principle of harmonious movement, carry out every task in the simplest, easiest manner, instead of treating the problem as an obstacle needing great effort."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSimplestWayYieldsKeysToAnyProblem a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Simplest-way habit yields access to solutions"@en, "Gewohnheit des Einfachsten erschließt Lösungen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving along least resistance opens the solutions encoded in the flow."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingSimplestWay ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKeysToAnyProblem ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStreamsOfOptimalLinks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Streams as chains of optimal links"@en, "Ströme als Ketten optimaler Glieder"@de ;
    skos:definition "Optimal alternatives of any action form streams like chains of optimal cause-and-effect links; each next step is the choice of the next link, which often does not match logical construction or everyday reasoning."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLogicAloneFails a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Logic alone rarely finds the optimal action"@en, "Logik allein findet selten die optimale Handlung"@de ;
    skos:definition "However careful, relying only on logic one rarely picks the optimal action, since the chain in the stream need not follow logic and the mind is always pressured (stress, anxiety, depression, overactivity) and distracted by pendulums, making it pushy."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: logic alone rarely finds the optimal action, bearing on pmc:TranserfingKeysToAnyProblem."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingBalanceBeforeFollowing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Balance and freedom from importance before following the flow"@en, "Gleichgewicht und Freiheit von Bedeutsamkeit vor dem Folgen"@de ;
    skos:definition "To choose the next link one must free oneself from the puppet strings and be compliant enough to follow: a state of balance and sufficient mindfulness to avoid projecting excessive importance; only once one feels in balance and harmony should one simply follow."@en ;
    skos:note "The dependent is choosing the next link by following the flow (pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow)."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Following the flow as detached administrator"@en, "Dem Fluss folgen als distanzierter Verwalter"@de ;
    skos:definition "In a state of balance, follow the flow: release the situation; be an objective observer, not a participant; act simply, neither slave nor master; have the inner Guardian nudge you whenever the mind attempts a 'sensible' but wilful decision; detach emotionally and watch your work from outside like an administrator; yield to simplicity."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFollowingTheFlowYieldsAtTheHelm a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Going with the flow yields the world meeting one halfway"@en, "Mit dem Fluss gehen bewirkt Entgegenkommen der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the flow with smooth, simple, detached action realises the stance at the helm and the world meeting one halfway."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm, pmc:TranserfingWorldMeetsYouHalfway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMultitudeOfSigns a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A multitude of guiding signs"@en, "Eine Vielzahl leitender Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When following the flow in balance, one is told one will notice many signs that guide one."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: a multitude of guiding signs, for pmp:TranserfingFollowingTheFlow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindLeadsToTheWaterfall a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "The mind, not the flow, leads to the waterfall"@en, "Der Verstand, nicht der Fluss, führt zum Wasserfall"@de ;
    skos:definition "It is the wilful mind rather than the alternatives flow that carries one to the waterfall's edge; things can be done far more simply than one thinks (e.g. searching the whole town for a shop that is next door, driven by importance)."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTechenieVariantov ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingStartWhereInclined a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Start with the task you feel like"@en, "Mit der Aufgabe beginnen, zu der man Lust hat"@de ;
    skos:definition "Facing a to-do list without a required order, do not deliberate: start with the task you feel most inclined to do, separating the mind from pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStartWhereInclinedYieldsAtTheHelm a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Going with the flow yields the world meeting one halfway"@en, "Mit dem Fluss gehen bewirkt Entgegenkommen der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the flow with smooth, simple, detached action realises the stance at the helm and the world meeting one halfway."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingStartWhereInclined ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm, pmc:TranserfingWorldMeetsYouHalfway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingADayWithTheFlow a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "A day of going with the flow"@en, "Ein Tag mit dem Fluss"@de ;
    skos:definition "For one whole day: for each problem, ask which approach is easiest and take it; when something or someone distracts you, do not rush to resist or bypass it, detach and watch what follows; for each new task ask how to do it as simply as possible and let it get done easily; when others propose something different or argue, do not jump to counter; activate the inner Guardian; observe first, act after; descend into the audience; do not rush to seize control; allow the game to unfold by itself under your supervision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingADayWithTheFlowYieldsAtTheHelm a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Going with the flow yields the world meeting one halfway"@en, "Mit dem Fluss gehen bewirkt Entgegenkommen der Welt"@de ;
    skos:definition "Following the flow with smooth, simple, detached action realises the stance at the helm and the world meeting one halfway."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingADayWithTheFlow ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingAtTheHelm, pmc:TranserfingWorldMeetsYouHalfway ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingADayWithTheFlowYieldsProblemsResolveThemselves a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting the flow run yields self-resolving problems"@en, "Den Fluss laufen lassen bewirkt Selbstlösung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not interfering with the flow lets minor problems resolve by themselves."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingADayWithTheFlow ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingProblemsResolveThemselves ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHelpfulAndSurprising a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Living this way proves helpful and surprising"@en, "Diese Lebensweise erweist sich als hilfreich und überraschend"@de ;
    skos:definition "After even one day of truly going with the flow one is told one will find it helpful and surprising, and will feel much better for not getting in the way of life's flow."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: living this way proves helpful and surprising, for pmp:TranserfingADayWithTheFlow."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Going With the Flow'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'
#

pmc:TranserfingKindsOfSigns a pm:Systematizing ;
    rdfs:label "Kinds of signs"@en, "Arten von Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The section distinguishes popular omens (no direct influence), guiding signs heralding turns in the flow, spontaneous casual phrases, and inner discomfort as the clearest sign; signs are sorted only into positive or negative."@en ;
    pm:compiledBy "Vadim Zeland" ;
    dcterms:date "2004"^^xsd:gYear ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHowOmensComeTrue a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "How omens come to be fulfilled"@en, "Wie Omen sich erfüllen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Popular omens arise from repeated observation and talk, yet often fail. Example (Russian custom of not returning for a forgotten item): the stereotype shadows the subconscious, fear unsettles the even flow, expectation of misfortune changes thought-energy parameters and shifts the person to a matching line; having let the event into their script, they experience it, which raises the share of omens that come true."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOmensActThroughResponse a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Omens act only through one's response"@en, "Omen wirken nur über die eigene Reaktion"@de ;
    skos:definition "Not the black cat but one's reaction to it has influence. Believing in omens lets them shape events; disbelieving yet doubting gives slight influence; total disregard gives none. One experiences what one admits into one's personal life script; the sceptic sees no confirmation in their layer."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingImmunityToOmens a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Immunity to omens"@en, "Unempfindlichkeit gegen Omen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A person who pays omens no attention at all is said to be entirely uninfluenced by them in their world-layer."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGuidingSign a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guiding sign"@en, "Wegweisendes Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "A guiding sign does not cause events but announces that the flow may be about to bend, i.e. a move to a markedly different life line; it appears only when such a shift is initiated or has just occurred, and is felt as an odd, slightly disturbing qualitative difference that reason cannot account for."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignVersusOrdinaryEvent a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Telling a sign from an ordinary event"@en, "Ein Zeichen von einem gewöhnlichen Ereignis unterscheiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "An event that neither alerts one nor feels qualitatively different indicates one is still on the same line; one that catches attention and seems unusual is probably a sign. Inattentive people miss even obvious signs; events of the same quality as the rest of the current line go unnoticed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingEscalatingWarnings a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Ignored warnings escalate to the encoded event"@en, "Ignorierte Warnungen eskalieren bis zum Ereignis"@de ;
    skos:definition "A shift to a very different line runs gradually through intermediate lines whose signs act as warnings of rising severity; if the first, second and third are ignored, the event coded into the shift's last line takes place."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: ignored warnings escalate to the encoded event, bearing on pmc:TranserfingGuidingSign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoPreciseDetail a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No precise detail; ambiguous feelings are unreliable"@en, "Keine genauen Details; mehrdeutige Gefühle sind unzuverlässig"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unambiguous interpretation is very hard, sometimes even whether something is a sign; expecting precise detail is pointless, and an ambiguous sensation makes any evaluation too subjective to trust."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingReadingASign a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Reading a sign by yes/no and feeling"@en, "Ein Zeichen per Ja/Nein und Gefühl lesen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Raise the inner Guardian's vigilance, note the sign and allow for it. Frame a question with a yes/no answer (will it work, will I be in time, is it dangerous) and reduce the interpretation to positive or negative, expecting no detail. If the sign brings unpleasant sensation, misgiving, surprise or anxiety, it signals a negative turn; if the feeling is ambiguous, do not interpret it. A sign may call for more care, a change of behaviour or stopping something."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReadingASignYieldsSensingTheComingTurn a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Sign reading yields a sense of the coming turn"@en, "Zeichenlesen bewirkt Gespür für die Wende"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reducing a sign to a yes/no felt verdict gives a hint of the forthcoming turn's quality."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSensingTheComingTurn ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSensingTheComingTurn a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Sensing the quality of the coming turn"@en, "Die Qualität der kommenden Wende spüren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signs are said to carry a hint of whether the next turn in the flow is favourable or not, giving at least an inkling of approaching sandbanks and rapids."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNeitherNegateNorInflateSigns a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Neither negate signs nor over-signify them"@en, "Zeichen weder verneinen noch überbewerten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signs should not be dismissed, nor allowed to cause worry by giving them too much significance."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTime a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Waking up in time"@en, "Rechtzeitig aufwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Signs are said to be able to wake one in time to see that one is acting for a destructive pendulum or against oneself, avoiding fatal mistakes made under a pendulum's zombifying anaesthesia."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReadingASignYieldsWakingUpInTime a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Treating even innocent signs as warnings yields timely waking"@en, "Auch harmlose Zeichen als Warnung nehmen bewirkt rechtzeitiges Aufwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reading signs as simple warnings keeps one vigilant against pendulums."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTime ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCautionWithoutAnxiety a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Caution must not turn into anxiety"@en, "Vorsicht darf nicht zu Angst werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Stay cautious and aware of surroundings, but without letting it degrade into anxiety and suspicion: be careful without worry, stay detached yet impeccable in all one does."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHeedingSpontaneousPhrases a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Heed spontaneous casual phrases"@en, "Spontane beiläufige Sätze beachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Ignore people pushing their opinion, but take seriously a casual recommendation uttered spontaneously and unplanned (e.g. 'don't forget your scarf'); do not discard passing remarks, and be willing to revise your view when someone unintentionally shows things differently."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSoulSpeaksWhenMindDozes a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "When the mind dozes the soul speaks"@en, "Wenn der Verstand döst, spricht die Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unplanned phrases bypass the analytical mind; with the mind drowsy or occupied, the soul talks, being in direct touch with the information field, which is why such phrases can be guiding signs."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHeedingSpontaneousPhrasesYieldsWakingUpInTime a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Heeding casual phrases yields timely waking"@en, "Beiläufiges beachten bewirkt rechtzeitiges Aufwachen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Acting on spontaneous advice spares later regret."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHeedingSpontaneousPhrases ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingWakingUpInTime ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Use inner discomfort as a decision sign"@en, "Inneres Unbehagen als Entscheidungszeichen nutzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When deciding, pause to listen for the morning-stars rustle and determine whether the decision pleases the soul. If you remembered too late, recall what you felt while deciding; a reluctant decision that left you cold counts as 'I don't feel good'. If still possible, reverse the decision."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSignYieldsKnowingTheUnrealisedSector a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Discomfort check yields knowing the right decision"@en, "Unbehagensprüfung bewirkt Wissen um die richtige Entscheidung"@de ;
    skos:definition "No one knows better than one's soul what a decision should be; consulting its comfort reveals it."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingKnowingTheUnrealisedSector ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRememberingTooLate a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Remembering too late; the mind overrides the soul's no"@en, "Zu spät erinnern; der Verstand übergeht das Nein der Seele"@de ;
    skos:definition "Assessing comfort is easy; the hard part is remembering to do it soon enough, because authoritative reason drowns the heart's whisper, hears the soul's timid 'no' yet pretends not to, and argues for its own 'yes' with sound judgement."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: remembering too late; the mind overrides the soul's no, bearing on pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingMindOverridesSoul a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Observing the mind override the soul as described"@en, "Beobachten, wie der Verstand die Seele übergeht"@de ;
    skos:definition "The reader is told to file these lines in memory and recall them at the next decision, and will then see the process run exactly as described."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: observing the mind override the soul as described, for pmp:TranserfingDiscomfortAsSign."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRecognisingTheInnerNo a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Recognising one's inner no"@en, "Das innere Nein erkennen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The ability to detect when the soul is actually saying 'no' behind a reasoned 'yes'."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingPersuasionTest a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Persuasion test for the inner no"@en, "Überredungstest für das innere Nein"@de ;
    skos:definition "Simple, reliable exercise: if a 'yes' needs self-persuasion and coaxing, your soul is saying 'no'; when the soul says 'yes', no self-persuasion is needed."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAssessingInnerComfort a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Assessing one's inner comfort"@en, "Das eigene innere Wohlbefinden einschätzen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind is held able to judge, even perfectly so the chapter summary says, how comfortable one feels inside; listening to one's gut and gauging comfort is called easy, the hard part being to remember it in time."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Added in reconciliation from pass B; the strong wording stands in the chapter summary, the plain one in the body."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPersuasionTestYieldsRecognisingTheInnerNo a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Persuasion test yields recognising the inner no"@en, "Überredungstest bewirkt Erkennen des inneren Nein"@de ;
    skos:definition "The need for self-persuasion reveals the soul's refusal."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingPersuasionTest ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingRecognisingTheInnerNo ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNotSignsEverywhere a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Do not look for signs everywhere"@en, "Nicht überall Zeichen suchen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Heed the world's signs without going overboard; reading meaning into every phenomenon (birds flying high) becomes absurd. It suffices to be aware of what one notices and keep in mind that it might be a sign."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLapsedVigilance a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Lapsed vigilance lets pendulums latch on"@en, "Nachlassende Wachsamkeit lässt Pendel zugreifen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The moment one forgets to be vigilant, pendulums latch on and one may become a victim of circumstance."@en ;
    skos:note "Condition of failure: lapsed vigilance lets pendulums latch on, bearing on pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingForegoingDiscomfort a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Forgo wishes and acts that bring discomfort"@en, "Auf Wünsche und Handlungen mit Unbehagen verzichten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Check carefully any desire or action that might alter your destiny's course; if it brings a negative gut feeling, or guilt, doubt or apprehension, do not do it whenever possible; make this a habit."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingGutFeelingMarksMindsDesire a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Negative gut feeling marks a desire of the mind"@en, "Negatives Bauchgefühl kennzeichnet einen Wunsch des Verstandes"@de ;
    skos:definition "A negative gut feeling about an intended act shows the desire stems from reason rather than the heart; reason's desires and acts are said always to be imposed by pendulums."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingIgnoredGutFeeling a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Ignoring a negative gut feeling can be deeply regretted"@en, "Ein negatives Bauchgefühl zu übergehen kann tief bereut werden"@de ;
    skos:definition "Usually nothing terrible follows from overriding a negative gut feeling, but sometimes one regrets it deeply."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingForegoingDiscomfort ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnotUntied a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Out of the knot"@en, "Aus dem Knoten heraus"@de ;
    skos:definition "The state of having been freed from a tangle into which a series of misplaced steps had tied one, in which one may be obliged to do uncomfortable things."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the integrator as the prior state of pmc:TranserfingKnotBeforeDiscomfortRule."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSimplifiedLife a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A greatly simplified life freed of many problems"@en, "Ein stark vereinfachtes, von vielen Problemen befreites Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "Habitually foregoing discomfort-laden desires and actions is said to greatly simplify life and free one from all sorts of problems."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingForegoingDiscomfortYieldsSimplifiedLife a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Foregoing discomfort yields a simpler life"@en, "Verzicht auf Unbehagen bewirkt ein einfacheres Leben"@de ;
    skos:definition "The habit of dropping what the soul dislikes removes many problems."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingForegoingDiscomfort ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingSimplifiedLife ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingKnotBeforeDiscomfortRule a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Untie the knot before applying the discomfort rule"@en, "Erst den Knoten lösen, dann die Unbehagensregel anwenden"@de ;
    skos:definition "When misplaced steps have tied one in a knot, the rule of foregoing discomfort can be applied with confidence only after the knot is untied and one is free of the complex situation."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior state, being out of the knot, is entered as pmc:TranserfingKnotUntied."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingForegoingDiscomfort ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingKnotUntied ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Inside the knot, rethinking desires may not suffice, since one may be obliged to do uncomfortable things such as lying or attending a job one hates." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsArePersonal a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Signs are personal and need no teaching"@en, "Zeichen sind persönlich und brauchen keine Lehre"@de ;
    skos:definition "Only the individual can interpret their own signs; observant of self and world, one understands them instinctively. One can manage without signs, whose meaning is never fully given; the one sign worth focusing on in decisions is gut feeling and intuition, the morning-stars rustle."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoImportanceOnUnclearSigns a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "No excess importance on unclear or negative signs"@en, "Keine überhöhte Bedeutsamkeit für unklare oder negative Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Beware of giving excess importance to unclear signs or to interpretations that would write negative content into one's personal life script."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingReadingASign ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingAvoidingSandbanks a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Avoiding sandbanks and rapids"@en, "Sandbänke und Stromschnellen meiden"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is said not to run aground or be swept down the rapids as long as one creates no excess potential."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingNoPotentialNoSandbank a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "No excess potential, no sandbank"@en, "Kein Überschusspotenzial, keine Sandbank"@de ;
    skos:definition "Safe passage on the flow depends on not creating excess potential."@en ;
    skos:note "The text names avoiding excess potential (pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial) as the condition; the practice this chapter gives for it is dropping inner and outer importance, so that practice stands as the prior step."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingAvoidingSandbanks ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingReducingImportance ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:prescribedOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Guiding Signs'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

#
# ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'
#

pmc:TranserfingFreedFromSolvingAndControlling a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Freeing the mind of solving and controlling"@en, "Den Verstand vom Lösen und Kontrollieren befreien"@de ;
    skos:definition "Streams in the flow can relieve the mind of two heavy burdens: having to solve problems by reason and having to control, if the mind lets itself be freed."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExplanationTheMindAccepts a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "A rational account for the mind"@en, "Eine Erklärung, die der Verstand annehmen kann"@de ;
    skos:definition "A more or less rational account of conclusions that seem irrational, offered so that the mind, which takes nothing on faith and demands proof, feels comfortable enough to let go; the author says he supplies such accounts for this reason."@en ;
    skos:note "Entered by the integrator as the prior step of pmc:TranserfingExplanationBeforeLettingGo."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingExplanationBeforeLettingGo a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "The mind needs an acceptable explanation to let go"@en, "Der Verstand braucht eine annehmbare Erklärung, um loszulassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Because the mind takes nothing on faith and needs a roughly rational account before it relaxes, the author supplies explanations of irrational-seeming conclusions."@en ;
    skos:note "The prior step, an explanation acceptable to the mind, is entered as pmc:TranserfingExplanationTheMindAccepts."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmc:TranserfingFreedFromSolvingAndControlling ;
    pm:priorStep pmc:TranserfingExplanationTheMindAccepts ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:statedNecessity ;
    pm:consequenceOfSkipping "Without such explanations the reader would hardly try the principles or read on." ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingProofFromPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Proof comes from one's own practice"@en, "Beweis kommt aus der eigenen Praxis"@de ;
    skos:definition "The author says Transurfing does not aim to describe the universe's structure; its explanations only soothe the incredulous mind, while the proof it demands the reader can supply by putting the principles into practice."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingCommonSenseTooLiterally a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Common sense followed too literally"@en, "Zu wörtlich befolgter gesunder Menschenverstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "Childhood training turns the mind into a soldier ready to explain, answer, assess, decide and control. Common sense is a minimal set of survival rules and is not to be discarded; its error is literal adherence, which keeps the mind from noticing what falls outside the rules."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingStreamsMorePurposeful a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Streams are more purposeful than the mind"@en, "Ströme sind zweckmäßiger als der Verstand"@de ;
    skos:definition "The streams have the purposefulness the mind seeks; nature being perfect, they hold more logic than the wisest reasoning, which still errs. The mind would err less if it let problems resolve themselves; relaxing one's controlling grip gives the world freedom and lets the flow take its course."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPressuringTheWorld a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pressuring the world creates obstacles"@en, "Druck auf die Welt erzeugt Hindernisse"@de ;
    skos:definition "Pressuring the world is futile and even dangerous; when the mind loses its feel for harmonious flow it builds excess potential, and that yields obstacles."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingHandlingObstacles a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Two-step handling of obstacles"@en, "Hindernisse in zwei Schritten behandeln"@de ;
    skos:definition "First, lower the importance you give the obstacle so that it fades by itself; second, if it does not yield to your efforts, go around it rather than force it."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingHandlingObstaclesYieldsObstaclesFade a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Lowering an obstacle's importance makes it fade"@en, "Bedeutsamkeit eines Hindernisses senken lässt es verblassen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Reduced importance dissolves the obstacle."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingHandlingObstacles ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingObstaclesFade ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObstaclesFade a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Obstacles fading of their own accord"@en, "Hindernisse verblassen von selbst"@de ;
    skos:definition "An obstacle whose importance is lowered is said to dissolve by itself."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSignsAppearWhenGoingAround a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Guiding signs appear when one goes around"@en, "Beim Umgehen erscheinen wegweisende Zeichen"@de ;
    skos:definition "If one moves around an unyielding obstacle, guiding signs are announced to appear and assist."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: guiding signs appear when one goes around, for pmp:TranserfingHandlingObstacles."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDeviationAsObstacle a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Deviation from the script read as obstacle"@en, "Abweichung vom Drehbuch als Hindernis gedeutet"@de ;
    skos:definition "The planning mind reads anything off-script as an obstacle and fights to force it back, worsening matters and generating new problems; the flow has no interest in ruining a life, which lacks purpose, but ill-designed actions can ruin it."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingSelfImportanceForbidsDeviation a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Self-importance forbids deviation"@en, "Selbstwichtigkeit verbietet Abweichung"@de ;
    skos:definition "Self-importance stops the mind from allowing any deviation from the original plan, which it reads as failure; unplanned gifts of life are accepted reluctantly ('I wanted a different toy'). Accepting that deviations have their place would make life joyful."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRegulatingHappiness a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Regulating one's own happiness"@en, "Das eigene Glück regulieren"@de ;
    skos:definition "Everyone is said to be able to regulate how happy they are; most set their minimum bar too high. The author distinguishes this from the slogan of simply being content, saying one can have the toy one wants most (deferred)."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    skos:note "A slogan about simply choosing to be happy is rejected as not Transurfing; unattributed, so not recorded as dispute."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControllingTheFlowItself a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Controlling the flow instead of one's movement in it"@en, "Den Fluss steuern statt der eigenen Bewegung darin"@de ;
    skos:definition "The mind's refusal of deviations keeps it from using ready solutions in the flow; its compulsion to control turns life into a fight with the flow. Its greatest error, and a main cause of most problems and disappointments, is steering the flow itself instead of its own motion in it. The stream of least resistance cannot create problems; the mind's madness does."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingWatchingTheMindControl a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "One day of observing the mind's control attempts"@en, "Einen Tag lang die Kontrollversuche des Verstandes beobachten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Activate the inner witness and for at least a day observe the mind's attempts to steer the flow: refusing offers, brushing people off, arguing, correcting others, rejecting proposed solutions, voicing dissatisfaction when expectations differ, getting angry, forcing what contradicts the script."@en ;
    skos:note "'Inner witness' appears to be used like the inner Guardian."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Move the weight from control to observation"@en, "Den Schwerpunkt von Kontrolle auf Beobachtung verlagern"@de ;
    skos:definition "Release your grip and give the flow more freedom without agreeing to everything: do not rush to dismiss, object, dispute, prove yourself, intervene, manage or criticise; let situations sort themselves out without active involvement or resistance; exercise detachment."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingObserveBeforeReleasing a pm:Presupposing ;
    rdfs:label "Observe the control habit before releasing it"@en, "Erst die Kontrollgewohnheit beobachten, dann lösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "The observation exercise is presented before the release exercise."@en ;
    pm:dependentStep pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation ;
    pm:priorStep pmp:TranserfingWatchingTheMindControl ;
    pm:prerequisiteStrength pm:presentationOrder ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingControlByReleasingControl a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Gaining control by releasing control"@en, "Kontrolle gewinnen durch Loslassen der Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Paradoxically, willingness to release control is said to yield greater command of a situation than before, since a detached observer is always better placed than the participant."@en ;
    skos:note "Counted as a capacity: a state or ability the text holds attainable."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFromControlToObservationYieldsControlByReleasingControl a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing grip yields greater control"@en, "Loslassen bewirkt größere Kontrolle"@de ;
    skos:definition "Moving from control to observation gives the observer's advantage."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingControlByReleasingControl ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingRetrospectiveView a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Surprise and the retrospective view"@en, "Überraschung und Rückschau"@de ;
    skos:definition "One is told one will be surprised, if not dumbfounded, by the result, and in hindsight will see that earlier control meant swimming against the flow, others' suggestions made sense, intervention was unnecessary, supposed obstacles were none, problems solved themselves, off-plan events were not so bad, chance phrases carried meaning, gut feelings warned, less energy was spent, and one feels quite happy."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: surprise and the retrospective view, for pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingFromControlToObservationYieldsProblemsResolveThemselves a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Releasing grip lets problems resolve"@en, "Loslassen lässt Probleme sich lösen"@de ;
    skos:definition "When one lets go, problems resolve satisfactorily without one knowing how."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingProblemsResolveThemselves, pmc:TranserfingFreedFromSolvingAndControlling ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingPendulumsProvokeTheFlow a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Pendulums provoke those who go with the flow"@en, "Pendel provozieren die, die mit dem Fluss gehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Going with the flow vexes pendulums, which hate streams because they follow minimal energy expenditure and yield no excess potential as fodder; so they provoke one at every step into thrashing the water. The only control worth exercising is over how strongly one projects inner and outer importance, which keeps the mind from letting go."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingVazhnost."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingUrgeToBeRight a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "The urge to prove oneself right"@en, "Der Drang, Recht zu behalten"@de ;
    skos:definition "Childhood self-assertion breeds the habit of proving one's significance and being right at any cost, even when the outcome is irrelevant to one's interests; this creates excess potential and conflict and can grow into a mania of compulsive control."@en ;
    skos:note "Bears on the system term pmc:TranserfingIzbytochnyPotentsial."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfArguments a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Let go when one's interests are not seriously at stake"@en, "Loslassen, wenn die eigenen Interessen nicht ernsthaft auf dem Spiel stehen"@de ;
    skos:definition "Unless your interests are seriously at risk, let the situation go and let others thrash the water; practise letting go consciously and act like a wise parent with difficult children instead of insisting on self-importance."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingLettingGoOfArgumentsYieldsFreeOfThePendulumsPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go yields freedom from pendulum provocation"@en, "Loslassen bewirkt Freiheit von Pendelprovokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declining to fight and correct starves pendulums of excess potential."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfArguments ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingReliefOverWinning a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Relief greater than winning the argument"@en, "Erleichterung größer als der Sieg im Streit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Conscious letting go is announced to bring more relief than proving one's point, and a sense of fulfilment at having moved on."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: relief greater than winning the argument, for pmp:TranserfingLettingGoOfArguments."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingOverzeal a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Overzeal at work"@en, "Übereifer bei der Arbeit"@de ;
    skos:definition "Excessive commitment to work is as harmful as neglect: throwing oneself too zealously into a coveted new post can exceed one's endurance, lower efficiency and at worst bring a nervous breakdown and the false conclusion that one cannot handle it."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTechenieVariantov ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingDisruptingEstablishedOrder a pm:Cautioning ;
    rdfs:label "Disrupting the established order"@en, "Die gewohnte Ordnung stören"@de ;
    skos:definition "Vigorous innovation that ignores the established order and changes colleagues' routine brings no good; initiative can then be punished, like slapping the water in a slow, even flow."@en ;
    pm:cautionsAbout pmc:TranserfingTechenieVariantov ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmp:TranserfingModerateCriticism a pm:Practicing ;
    rdfs:label "Rule of moderate criticism"@en, "Regel maßvoller Kritik"@de ;
    skos:definition "Neither silence nor head down: get annoyed or reprimand someone only if they bother you directly and only if the criticism will improve the situation; never criticise what is past and unchangeable; otherwise go with the flow by shifting from control to observation, without literally agreeing with everyone."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingModerateCriticismYieldsFreeOfThePendulumsPower a pm:Yielding ;
    rdfs:label "Letting go yields freedom from pendulum provocation"@en, "Loslassen bewirkt Freiheit von Pendelprovokation"@de ;
    skos:definition "Declining to fight and correct starves pendulums of excess potential."@en ;
    pm:byPractice pmp:TranserfingModerateCriticism ;
    pm:yieldsCapacity pmc:TranserfingFreeOfThePendulumsPower ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .

pmc:TranserfingModerationWithPractice a pm:Conceptualizing ;
    rdfs:label "Moderation comes with practice"@en, "Maß kommt mit der Übung"@de ;
    skos:definition "No need to worry about getting the balance right; a healthy sense of moderation is promised to come with practice."@en ;
    skos:note "Sign of success announced in advance: moderation comes with practice, for pmp:TranserfingModerateCriticism, pmp:TranserfingFromControlToObservation."@en ;
    pm:attestedBy pm:textualAttestation ;
    pm:withinTradition pmt:Transerfing ;
    pm:fromWork pmw:TranserfingStupen1 ;
    dcterms:source "Vadim Zeland, Transerfing real'nosti, Stupen' I: Prostranstvo variantov (2004), ch. VI The Alternatives Flow, section 'Letting Go'; read in the English translation of the combined edition, Reality Transurfing: steps 1-5 (OJSC Ves Publishing Group, 2012), translator not named, which carries no page numbers" .
